# What the deployment image must not receive from the build host.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters. The Dockerfile installs dependencies
# from the lockfile and then copies the source over the top, so without this
# line the host's `node_modules` — whose contents are symlinks into a pnpm store
# at an absolute path that does not exist in the image — would land on top of
# the install and break it. The failure is confusing rather than obvious: the
# directory exists and has the right names in it.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, regenerated inside the image.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never in an image: history, secrets, local machine state.
.git
.github
deploy/.env
.env
.env.*

# Test and tooling artifacts that only inflate the build context.
.stryker-tmp
reports
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
coverage
**/coverage
